# Yozora Cursor ingest workflow

You are a Cursor agent doing **labeled** Dreamscape work. You are not Yukimi
(`UiharuKazari2008`) and you are not Menma. Auth as `grok.cursor` only.

Yozora is Gitea 1.25.5 at `https://yozora.bluesteel.737.jp.net/`.
Canonical repo: `DreamScape/StaticForge`. There is **no** project/board REST API.
Rook cards every issue on the org board via the web UI. After you create an
issue, comment `@grok.rook please card`.

## Auth

- PAT lives on the Dreamscape server (Cursor CLI): `/home/kanmi/.secrets/yozora-grok.cursor.token`
- Env: `YOZORA_TOKEN` from that file.
- User: `grok.cursor`. Least privilege: `read:repository`, `write:issue`.
- **Never** use `UiharuKazari2008`, `grok.rook`, `grok.menma`, kanmi git-credentials, or any other token.
- Never put the token in an issue comment, commit, or chat.

Header: `Authorization: token $YOZORA_TOKEN`

Look up label IDs every session. Do not hardcode them.

```
GET /api/v1/repos/DreamScape/StaticForge/labels?limit=50
```

## What you may pick up

Open issues on `DreamScape/StaticForge` (or another repo named in the issue) that have **`cursor-agent` or `cursor-take`**.

```
GET /api/v1/repos/DreamScape/StaticForge/issues?state=open&labels=cursor-agent&limit=50
GET /api/v1/repos/DreamScape/StaticForge/issues?state=open&labels=cursor-take&limit=50
```

- **`cursor-agent`**: fan-out lane. Cheap ingest. Not Menma's private pile.
- **`cursor-take`**: assigned to an employee (Menma, Chiyo, or someone else) **and** Cursor should still take the work if it sees the issue. Do not skip just because `assignee` is `grok.menma` / `grok.chiyo`. Take it.

**Hard stops (both labels):**

- Label `greg` (old name `ceo` if it ever reappears): stop. Yukimi in Cursor. Do not implement.
- `ui-review` without Yukimi's explicit approve-on-issue: stop and comment that Rook must gate it.
- `status:in-progress` **and** the assignee is a person who is not you, **unless** the issue also has `cursor-take`.
- Do not take work that is already in flight without `cursor-take`.

`greg` is major/design. Never assign `greg` issues to yourself, Menma, or Chiyo. If you accidentally open one, comment and stop.

## Time tracker (required)

Gitea stopwatch, per issue you are working:

Start **as soon as you begin** (including planning, reading, or first edit):

```
POST /api/v1/repos/DreamScape/StaticForge/issues/{index}/stopwatch/start
```

Stop when the task is **fully done**. If you are waiting for Yukimi or Rook to verify, **still stop**. Do not leave a timer running through review.

```
POST /api/v1/repos/DreamScape/StaticForge/issues/{index}/stopwatch/stop
```

Only one stopwatch can run at a time for `grok.cursor`. If you switch issues, stop the old one before starting the new one.

```
GET /api/v1/user/stopwatches
```

If start returns that a stopwatch already exists on another issue, stop that one first. Do not delete tracked time.

## Labels (update them as you go)

Status labels map to board columns. Keep them true.

| When | Do |
| --- | --- |
| You start | add `status:in-progress`; remove `status:ready`, `status:triage`, `status:inbox` |
| Done, waiting for verify | add `status:review`; remove `status:in-progress`; **stop timer** |
| Blocked on someone else | add `status:blocked`; remove `status:in-progress`; stop timer; comment the blocker |
| Balloon / needs Yukimi | stop timer; comment what you found; **do not** self-tag `greg`. Rook retags. |

Replace labels with the issue label API (IDs from the labels list). Keep `cursor-agent` / `cursor-take`, `credit:menma`, type, and priority unless Rook said to change them.

```
PUT /api/v1/repos/DreamScape/StaticForge/issues/{index}/labels
{"labels": [<id>, ...]}
```

Do **not** close the issue. Rook closes after review.

## Planning always has a Yozora issue

Do not keep a plan only in the Cursor session.

- If the work already has an issue: write the plan into that issue (body or a `## Plan` comment) and **PATCH the body as the plan changes**.
- If you are about to plan work that has **no** issue: **create the issue first**, then plan there.
- Start the stopwatch when planning starts; stop it when planning is finished, even if you are waiting for Yukimi to approve the plan.

Title new plan issues `[Plan] <short name>`. Link them to the parent issue in both bodies.

## New issues for extra work

If you discover work that was **not** in the original request (a missing slice, a bug, a follow-up, a new file that needs its own ticket): **file a new Yozora issue**. Do not silently expand the current ticket. Do not dump it into an unrelated PR.

```
POST /api/v1/repos/DreamScape/StaticForge/issues
{
  "title": "<short, specific>",
  "body": "<why, scope, parent issue #, how to verify>"
}
```

Then set labels (IDs from the list):

- Always: a `type:*` (`type:bug` / `type:feature` / `type:infra` / `type:research`) and `status:inbox`
- Ingest-sized / can wait: `cursor-agent` (and `credit:menma` if Menma found it)
- Assigned to an employee but Cursor should still take it: `cursor-take`
- Major or design (Yukimi in Cursor): `greg` and assignee `UiharuKazari2008` — then **stop**, do not implement
- New undesigned UI: `ui-review` and **stop** until Yukimi approves on the issue

Comment on the parent: `Split off #<n> for <reason>. @grok.rook please card.`

Do not assign new issues to `UiharuKazari2008` unless they are `greg`.

## Comments (required)

Start work (after stopwatch start + in-progress):

```
POST /api/v1/repos/DreamScape/StaticForge/issues/{index}/comments
{"body": "Starting. Cursor agent (`grok.cursor`), not impersonating Yukimi. Timer on."}
```

When done, **stop the timer**, set `status:review`, and comment **exactly this shape** so Rook can verify and credit Menma:

```
## Done
- Commit: `<sha>` (branch / main as applicable)
- Files: <paths>
- What changed: <one short paragraph>
- How to verify: <commands or click-path>
- PM2 / SW: bounced | SW notified | not needed (say which)
- Timer: stopped (waiting for verify counts as stop)
- credit: grok.menma
- lines: added N / deleted M  (git show --numstat on the ship commit(s); this is Menma's cake math)
```

Do **not** close the issue. Do not reopen `greg` work.

## Change JSON /agent work is not UI

Unless the issue says otherwise, StaticForge Change JSON and `POST /agent/*` tasks are **application JSON + docs**:

- Optional fields on the existing change payload
- Echo on `GET /agent/session/state`
- Update `docs/studio-change-json.md` and `docs/client-api/agent-session.md`

**Do not** add a visible grid, dialog, window, or other chrome for character position, layout, or similar. Prompt-text placement is not a substitute for a JSON field, and a new UI is not in scope unless `ui-review` is approved.

Characters today are `action: replace` + `index` only (`docs/studio-change-json.md`). A position/cell/x-y field is extra JSON on that object, not a Studio layout editor.

## Scope discipline

If the change balloons (touches many unrelated files, needs a design call, or would eat a long review): **stop the timer**, comment what you found, leave the tree clean or on a branch, ping nothing else. Rook will retag `greg` or split the ticket.

Without `cursor-take`, do not take in-flight Menma/Chiyo work. Do not "help" by rewriting adjacent systems.

## Credit

Every ship comment includes `credit: grok.menma`. Menma gets the cake for Cursor-landed work. Do not assign the issue to `UiharuKazari2008` unless it is `greg` (and then you should not be shipping it).

Issues labeled `credit:menma` were discovered by Menma; all work and line counts go to her even though Cursor shipped them. Do not close. Rook closes.

